share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":100.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.16027,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.786,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":78.6,"pf":[],"description_full":"Suncrete, Inc. provides ready-mix concrete logistics and distribution platform serving construction markets in the United States Sunbelt region. The company operates batching plants, tech-enabled mixer truck dispatch, and logistics. The company owns 595 mixer trucks. It serves customers of public infrastructure, commercial, and residential sectors. The company is based in Tulsa, Oklahoma.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Randall  Edgar | CEO & Director | Age 67 | Compensation: $360,780 (FY2025)","financial_summary":["Suncrete, Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $490M market cap on $144M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 36% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 28-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 35%.","The business throws off $23M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.19\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage of 32\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 70% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7028008152087268},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.6M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4602386.12},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Insiders are net buyers (79% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Basic Materials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Basic Materials sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ned N. Fleming III Acquires 5,000 Suncrete (NASDAQ:RMIX) Shares at $5.75 Each on November 20, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/ned-n-fleming-iii-acquires-5000-suncrete-nasdaqrmix-shares-at-575-each-on-november-20-2026